{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
  "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress has provided that certain aliens, including those with good moral character, are eligible for voluntary departure. Congress has also provided that all aliens may file one motion to reopen raising new facts within 90 days."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there are 10,000 motions to reopen filed, but that's for all aliens, for all removal proceedings. Since voluntary departure is roughly 10 percent of all removals, we estimate that'S roughly a thousand motions to reopen filed by voluntary departure recipients."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you have a final order of removal, yes, you can file for a stay once you have a final order."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: That's by regulation, though, that he can't, he cannot pursue that from out of the country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Meade",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MEADE: Even with voluntary departure. Leaving the country triggers these bars. Once you're outside the country you cannot reapply for admission for in some cases up to 10 years, and that precludes the ability to leave the country and seek the relief, even if you have a marriage to a United States citizen, even if there are extreme circumstances in a particular case that need to be addressed and that would be addressed under a motion to reopen."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The filing of a motion to reopen does not automatically suspend the obligation of an alien to leave the United States within the time that was specified in the Board's order granting permission to depart voluntarily."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The filing of a motion to reopen does not automatically suspend the obligation of an alien to leave the United States within the time that was specified in the Board's order granting permission to depart voluntarily. The grant of voluntary departure reflects an exchange of benefits between the government and the alien and Petitioner's automatic tolling rule would greatly subvert that reciprocal arrangement by giving the alien the unilateral and automatic ability to extend the substantive terms of the immigration relief the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Okay, but isn't the question in this case whether what Congress did was as modest as you say? Because if it is as modest as you say, then in at least a substantial category of cases in which a motion to reopen will be filed, it will in fact be no time in the real world to act on that motion before the voluntary departure date. And the question is did Congress really intend a right to reopen that is as modest as that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And one question that Justice Breyer asked about, what if reopening is denied would the automatic tolling rule continue?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Board",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "resolved I think only about 55 percent of those within 90 days."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. KNEEDLER",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0002-0008",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's an automatic tolling period."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why isn't the solution to withdraw, relinquish the voluntary departure?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOUTER",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there any reason he could not unilaterally relinquish the voluntary departure status as distinct from having to get approval from the Board or bureaucrat?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. KNEEDLER)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Board's order grants him permission to voluntary depart and says the following consequences will attach if you do not. Nothing in the Board's order allows him to withdraw."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you know what percentage of these motions to reopen are granted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government (Mr. MEADE)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government's arguments on the statutory interpretation in this case are undermined by its own proposed rule for at least five reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't it your position that the statute requires tolling?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0003-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "This Court -- as to your question, Justice Alito, on the -- with the regulations with respect to withdraw in this case, the agency is silent on that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1181",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0feedba992cc4206108d209d55fcfc845a2e9ea7385e6c3720aaf24aa248cec6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0feedba992cc-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Not if it has 10,000 of these a year, as you told me in your opening argument."
    },
    {
